From edefd416f08a91610d8146813be0a52d860cf5ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben Vanik <ben.vanik@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 23:02:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [Loom/AMDGPU] Consume VMEM VGPR sources at issue

Ordinary AMDGPU VMEM stores consume VGPR address and payload operands
when the instruction issues. Stop projecting store-completion leases
over those operands so allocation can reuse their registers while stores
remain outstanding. Preserve scalar memory-source leases, gfx125x XCNT
source lifetimes, memory ordering, and final store completion.

When the corrected lifetime produces a different legal allocation, frame
construction can require value repair followed by several
spill-materialization batches. Bound those independent convergence
processes separately, while retaining total repair statistics and
checkpoint-based bounded memory.

Backport of upstream 30246a9d6204868590fbd3a44d57735dd5d43c18 (merged
via 7a2cc8306, #425) onto 5927b0e0 and the LSE series. No earlier upstream
commit is needed. The series already carries #1398, which keeps spill
materialization out of the frame repair budget, so of this change's
frame.c part only the removal of the budget guard on pair replication
remains. LSE's own fixtures follow the same register reuse: the
low_vmem_latency_schedule case (from the series' load-latency change) and
the live_in_split_follows_entry_preamble allocation case now reuse a
stored VGPR once its store issues; the workitem id's v0 stays intact.
